## Config
### Environment Variables

| Variable | Description | Default | Required | Notes |
|----------|----------|----------|----------|----------|
| `ESI_USER_AGENT` | ESI client user agent string. | -  | ✅ | Must follow [ESI best practices](https://developers.eveonline.com/docs/services/esi/best-practices/#user-agents). |
| `ESI_CACHE_STRATEGY` | Cache strategy to use for ESI client. | `memory` | ❌ | Options: `redis`, `memory`, `none`. |
| `ESI_REDIS_HOST`   | Redis host address. | - | ✅\* | Required only if cache strategy is `redis`. |
| `ESI_REDIS_USER`   | Redis username. | - | ❌ | Optional. |
| `ESI_REDIS_PASSWORD` | Redis password. | - | ❌ | Optional. |
| `ESI_REDIS_PORT`   | Redis port. | `6379`   | ❌ | Optional. |
| `ESI_REDIS_TLS`    | Whether to use TLS for Redis connection. | `false`  | ❌ | Optional. |

> You can copy these variables into a `.env` file or use the provided `.env.example` as a template.

### `EsiClient` Options
The `EsiClient` class supports several optional configuration options that let you customize its behavior:

| Option | Type | Default | Description |
|---------|---------|---------|---------|
| `bypassCache`     | `boolean`      | `true`  | Whether to bypass caching.                                 |
| `middleware`      | `Middleware[]` | `[]`    | Array of middleware functions to customize requests. For examples of middleware please see the middleware folder in the repository |
| `retries`         | `number`       | `3`     | Number of retry attempts for failed requests. Time between retires is exponential. |
| `userAgentOverride` | `string`     | `undefined` | Overrides the entire User-Agent header for requests.      |

