This package **does not** implement the full EvE SSO flow, however a function under the `sso` class is provided to get an up to date access token for the esi, as seen below. It is the responsibility of the application to handle the issuing and storage of refresh tokens.

```typescript
import { getEsiClient } from '@indipsyno/esi'

const esi = getEsiClient()

const token = await esi.sso.getAccessToken({
    clientId: "Your Client ID",
    clientSecret: "Your Client Secret",
    refreshToken: "Characters Refresh Token"
})
```

